Velocity models: sources, credits and licenses
==============================================

Each array stores float32 speed in m/s with axes (depth, horizontal position).
The experiment area-resamples the whole array to 70 x 70 cells at 10 m. Every
run archive records the SHA-256 of the file it read. Each conversion below was
checked against every velocity sample of the upstream distribution.


marmousi.npy
------------

Native shape 751 x 2,301 (z, x), 4 m spacing on both axes.

Source: IFP Marmousi, created by the Institut Francais du Petrole. Decoded from
the XDR float32 samples in Madagascar's marmvel.hh in depth-fast order; the
values are already in m/s.

  Model history:  https://ahay.org/RSF/book/data/marmousi/paper.pdf
  Source samples: https://ahay.org/data/marm/marmvel.hh


overthrust.npy
--------------

Native shape 187 x 801 (z, x), 25 m spacing on both axes.

Source: SEG/EAGE 3-D Overthrust model, CD1 file overthrust.vites, read as
big-endian float32 with shape (z, y, x) = (187, 801, 801). This file is the 2-D
section volume[:, 454, :] (zero-based y index 454), converted to NumPy. No
velocity values were changed.

  Distribution: https://zenodo.org/records/23469292

