bp_salt.npy
-----------

Native shape 1,911 x 5,395 (z, x), 6.25 m depth and 12.5 m horizontal spacing.

Source: 2004 BP velocity benchmark, exact velocity file
vel_z6.25m_x12.5m_exact.segy.gz. IBM floats decoded to float32, traces
transposed to (z, x), values kept in m/s.

  Distribution: https://zenodo.org/records/23469290

The BP 2004 velocity data are provided courtesy of BP. Acknowledge BP and
Frederic Billette in publications and presentations that use these data.

Cite: Billette, F. J., Brandsberg-Dahl, S., 2005. The 2004 BP velocity
benchmark. 67th Annual International Meeting, EAGE, Expanded Abstracts, B035.

BP's terms require its original documentation to accompany the data whenever
it is passed on, with any change recorded in README_Modification. Those files
are in data/bp2004/: the documentation and terms (2004_Benchmark_READMES.pdf),
the modification record (README_Modification) and the abstract
(eage_abstract.pdf).


seam.npy
--------

Native shape 1,501 x 1,751 (z, x), 10 m depth and 20 m horizontal spacing.

Source: SEAM Phase I elastic 2-D model subset, east-west profile at North
23,900 m. The P-wave file SEAM_Vp_Elastic_N23900.sgy decoded and transposed to
(z, x), in m/s. No velocity values were changed.

  SEG open data:         https://seg.org/seam/open-data/
  Original distribution: https://seam-open-data.s3.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/Phase+I/SEAM_I_2D_Model.zip

